# Milestone: M3
# Covers: passing NULL Realm to urbi_run_chunk reuses the global default Realm;
#         consecutive chunks in the same slot see shared bindings.
#
# defer-to: T39 (chk runner host-driver extension) + T20 (Strand C API)
#
# Reason: chk runner uses the standalone urbi binary which manages a single
# global Realm internally. There is no host hook to call urbi_run_chunk(vm, NULL, ...)
# to demonstrate the NULL→global-Realm coercion.
# Realm-side semantics are already verified by tests/unit/test_realm.c (T14)
# and tests/unit/test_chunk_apis.c::run_chunk_null_realm_uses_global (T16).
#
# When T39 lands, implement this fixture by adding a host-driver section that:
# 1. Calls urbi_run_chunk(vm, NULL, chunk1, ...) to bind x=42 in global Realm.
# 2. Calls urbi_run_chunk(vm, NULL, chunk2, ...) to read x.
# 3. Verifies chunk2 sees x=42.
#
# Pseudo-host-driver (activate at T39):
#   UChunk *c1 = urbi_parse(vm, "var x = 42");
#   UChunk *c2 = urbi_parse(vm, "x");
#   urbi_run_chunk(vm, NULL, c1, URBI_CHUNK_NORMAL);
#   urbi_run_chunk(vm, NULL, c2, URBI_CHUNK_NORMAL);
#   --- expected output (from chunk2) ---
#   [00000001] 42
